{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And all the water that was in the river turned to blood.</b> The river did not become blood except temporarily, and immediately the fish died because of the blood, and afterward the river returned to its original state. And what is written, 'and the Egyptians could not drink of the water of the river' — not because it was blood, for we do not find that they sought to have the plague removed, but because 'the fish that were in the river died, and the river became foul.' And a proof for this: 'and the magicians did so' — if the river had not returned to its original state, how could they do so? And one may say that the plague that Moses performed was on the waters visible to people, while the magicians dealt with those under the ground. And a proof for this: 'and all the Egyptians dug around the river' — for those waters were not turned to blood, only the waters of the river."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:30.534847160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}